**`ZenEnhancement::StillImageTune` recipe v1 — measured on a 42-image
k-means-diverse imazen-26 subset.** The bundle = C's tune-IQ overrides
(`apply_tune_overrides`: QM on + still levels, sharpness 7, variance boost
strength 3 / curve 2, `max_tx_size` 32 at qp<=45, `screen_content_mode = 3`)
with `variance_octile` pinned to 8 instead of the default 5. Everything else
that tune IQ installs is untouched; caller-set knobs survive the recipe.

date:   2026-09-19
host:   r7900x — AMD Ryzen 9 7900X (Zen 4), no hw perf counters
        (perf_event_paranoid=4) — wall clock only, spawn overhead included
        identically in every arm.
port:   `ba8d35e52` + working tree (SvtTune enum, with_tune,
        StillImageTune). C reference `3115c0c1b`.
rustc:  1.98.1
data:   benchmarks/still_image_tune_v1_round1_2026-09-19.tsv (1512 cells)
        benchmarks/still_image_tune_v1_round2_2026-09-19.tsv (756 cells)
        benchmarks/still_image_tune_v1_subset_2026-09-19.tsv (42 images)
        benchmarks/still_image_tune_v1_sweep_*.py (harness)

========================= 1. SUBSET =========================

42 images, 21 top-level classes, exactly 2 per class — the class's two
largest k-means clusters' representatives from
`imazen-26-png-v3/manifests/kmeans_k300_representatives.tsv` where present,
else the next distinct representative of that class. Git-LFS materialized
(`git lfs pull`); all 42 verified PNG-signatured, not pointer stubs.

Protocol per cell: `identity_run "crop:<png>" 512 512 <qp> 6 <out>` — the
encoder's own `crop:` path center-crops to 512² and converts RGB→I420 with
its integer BT.601-limited transform; `<out>.yuv` records the exact samples
encoded. Then `aomdec -o <out>.y4m <out>.obu`, y4m→I420, inverse BT.601 to
PNG, `fast-ssim2-cli image <src.png> <dec.png>`. Encode ms is wall clock of
the whole `identity_run` process (~0.3 s spawn+PNG decode overhead included
in every arm alike). qp ∈ {20, 32, 44}, preset 6, all-intra.

2268 cells total; 0 encode errors, 0 decode errors — every stream aomdec
decodes. Sanity anchors: identical PNG pair scores 100.0; the C encoder on
the stone-texture cell produces BYTE-IDENTICAL output to the port (24319 B,
same −472 score — the content is adversarial, not a scoring bug).

========================= 2. HEADLINE — recipe vs plain tune IQ =========================

Matched-qp deltas, `st_oct8` (= shipped recipe v1) vs `t3`, 126 cells:

    bytes:   q20 −9.8%  q32 −15.4%  q44 −18.8%   (medians)
             pooled p25/p50/p75 = −20.7 / −13.0 / −6.9
    ssim2:   p25/p50/p75 = −0.010 / +0.011 / +0.136   (≈ no change)
    cells:   108 dominant (fewer bytes AND ≥ score) / 0 losing
    time:    1473 ms median vs t3's 1901 ms — ~22% FASTER than tune IQ
             (fewer boosted SBs → less VB/MD work)
    classes: NEGATIVE in all 21 classes at q32 (−2.9% patents … −25.0%
             nature) — no class regression.

Mechanism: `variance_octile` picks which octile of the sorted per-SB
variance distribution anchors the boost curve. Octile 8 restricts the boost
to the top-variance octile only, trimming most of tune IQ's matched-qp byte
inflation while keeping the rest of the bundle (QM, sharpness 7, max-tx
cap, forced screen detection) intact.

Ablations swept (round 1 + 2, all on top of the IQ base): octile 6 (−4.5%
med) and 7 (−9.9%) — same direction, smaller; vb_strength 4 = WORSE
(+3.8% med, 27 losing cells); ac_bias 0.6/1.0/2.0 ≈ neutral (Δssim2 med
≤ +0.017, not pinned); oct8+vb4 and oct8+ac10 no better than oct8 alone.

========================= 3. HONEST BASELINE — vs default PSNR tune =========================

At matched qp on THIS corpus the IQ-based bundles still spend more bytes
than default tune 1 for ~no measured ssim2 change:

    t3  vs t1:  +33.3% med bytes (p25 +9.9, p75 +81.5), Δssim2 −0.078,
                7 dominant / 64 losing cells, +40% encode time.
    st_oct8 vs t1: +9.3% med bytes at q44 … +12.5% at q32 (pooled p50
                +13.7%), Δssim2 −0.077, 14 dominant / 56 losing.
    t2  vs t1:  −2.2% med bytes at Δssim2 ≈ 0 (81 dom / 1 loss) — a
                modest clean win, but t2 is SSIM-rdmult only, not a still
                bundle.
    t4  vs t1:  +29.1% med bytes, Δssim2 −0.070.

So the bundle's value is strictly measured AGAINST TUNE IQ, which it beats
everywhere; against the shipping default it is a measured trade (more bits,
IQ's feature set), NOT a free win on this protocol — which is exactly why
it ships as an explicit opt-in enhancement and not an inferred default.

========================= 4. CAVEATS =========================

- Operating point: 512² center-crops of 1–12 MP sources at qp 20–44 land
  deep in ssim2's negative range (t1@q32 medians run −12.6 to −240 per
  class). The metric functions (sanity anchors above) but Δssim2≈0 partly
  reflects saturation; matched-qp BYTES are the reliable signal here. A
  prior single-photo probe (complete scene at 512², q20) showed t3 beating
  t1 (−8% bytes AND +0.3 ssim2) — the IQ bundle's value is
  content/protocol-dependent, not universal.
- Formal BD-rate was computed but discarded: on flat/saturated content the
  ssim2-vs-rate curve is non-monotone and interpolation explodes (e.g.
  renders showed +222% artifacts). Matched-qp deltas used instead.
- enc_ms includes process spawn + PNG decode; ratios are fair, absolute
  numbers are not codec-time-pure.
- n=2 per class: per-class rows are indicative, pooled medians are the
  claim.
- Recipe pins are env-sweepable (`SVT_FORK_*` survives the tune override),
  so the bundle remains tunable without a new enum version.
